{
  "n": 2,
  "title": "Everyday verbs",
  "sub": "Present tense: -ar, -er, -ir",
  "can": "Say where you live, what you do and what you're learning, and ask other people the same.",
  "mins": 14,
  "doneText": "You can now build the present tense of any regular verb and talk about your everyday life.",
  "skills": {
    "ar-verbs": "Present tense: -ar verbs",
    "er-ir-verbs": "Present tense: -er and -ir verbs",
    "who": "Who is doing it: verb endings",
    "no-do": "Questions without \"do\"",
    "vosotros": "Vosotros forms"
  },
  "discover": {
    "intro": "None of these sentences has a word for \"I\" or \"we\". See if you can work out how Spanish shows who is doing it.",
    "groups": [
      {
        "label": "One person (I)",
        "tone": "blue",
        "lines": [
          [
            "Hablo inglés.",
            "I speak English."
          ],
          [
            "Vivo en Londres.",
            "I live in London."
          ],
          [
            "Como mucha fruta.",
            "I eat lots of fruit."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "A group (we)",
        "tone": "orange",
        "lines": [
          [
            "Hablamos inglés.",
            "We speak English."
          ],
          [
            "Vivimos en Londres.",
            "We live in London."
          ],
          [
            "Comemos mucha fruta.",
            "We eat lots of fruit."
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "question": "So how do you know who is doing it?",
    "options": [
      "The end of the verb: -o means I, -mos means we.",
      "The word order: the person always comes last.",
      "You can't. Spanish speakers guess from context."
    ],
    "answer": 0,
    "nudge": "Not quite. Compare the verbs only: hablo and hablamos, vivo and vivimos. What changes?",
    "reveal": "The ending tells you who. That is why Spanish usually drops yo, tú and nosotros. To build a regular verb, take off -ar, -er or -ir and add the ending for the person:",
    "hooks": [
      {
        "title": "-AR verbs: hablar",
        "tone": "blue",
        "rows": [
          [
            "-o",
            "yo",
            "hablo",
            "I speak"
          ],
          [
            "-as",
            "tú",
            "hablas",
            "you speak"
          ],
          [
